
# 1. What is Express Router?

### Answer

Express Router is a mini version of the Express application that helps organize routes into separate modules. Instead of writing all routes in `app.js`, routes are grouped by feature (users, products, auth), making the project cleaner and easier to maintain. 

### Example

```javascript
const express = require("express");
const router = express.Router();

router.get("/", getUsers);

module.exports = router;
```

---

# 2. Difference between `app` and `router`?

| app                      | router                      |
| ------------------------ | --------------------------- |
| Main Express application | Mini Express application    |
| Used once                | Can create multiple routers |
| Starts the server        | Organizes related routes    |

