# 9. What are REST API Best Practices?

### Answer

Some important REST API best practices are:

* Use nouns instead of verbs (`/users`, not `/getUsers`)
* Use proper HTTP methods (GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE)
* Return meaningful HTTP status codes
* Validate request data
* Support pagination and filtering
* Keep endpoints consistent
* Version APIs (e.g., `/api/v1/users`)

These practices make APIs easier to use, maintain, and scale. ([w4school.in][3])

