# 10. How do you handle asynchronous errors in Express?

### Answer

Asynchronous errors can be handled using `try...catch`, centralized error-handling middleware, or helper libraries such as `express-async-handler`. In Express 5, rejected promises from async route handlers are automatically forwarded to error-handling middleware. ([InterviewPrep][4])

### Example

```javascript
try {
    const user = await User.findById(id);
} catch (err) {
    next(err);
}
```

